1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,540
Integration.

2
00:00:01,540 --> 00:00:06,330
Protecting wild animals. A.

3
00:00:06,330 --> 00:00:11,160
Daniel is reading two articles about wild animals.

4
00:00:11,160 --> 00:00:15,815
Read with him and answer the questions below.

5
00:00:15,815 --> 00:00:18,690
We live in the Arctic.

6
00:00:18,690 --> 00:00:25,980
We are the biggest meat-eaters on land, and we often have to travel a long way to find food.

7
00:00:25,980 --> 00:00:30,770
The Earth is becoming warmer, and the Arctic ice is melting.

8
00:00:30,770 --> 00:00:35,430
This makes it more difficult for us to survive.

9
00:00:35,430 --> 00:00:45,700
Today, there are about 22,000 to 31,000 of us on Earth, and our number may still drop.

10
00:00:45,700 --> 00:00:55,080
We are the largest animals on the planet, the ocean is our home, and we can live up to 90 years.

11
00:00:55,080 --> 00:01:01,360
In the past, humans hunted us, and there were very few of us left.

12
00:01:01,360 --> 00:01:07,250
Now, it is against the law to hunt us, but we are still at risk.

13
00:01:07,250 --> 00:01:10,520
Big ships often hit and hurt us.

14
00:01:10,520 --> 00:01:18,050
What's more, the ocean water is getting warmer, and we may not have enough food to eat in the future.

15
00:01:18,050 --> 00:01:22,600
It is harder for us to live long and healthy lives than before.
